   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of waste management system established in municipality</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">5</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">At least in 2 municipalities</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Agreement for Partnership on municipal waste management is establishment with two municipalities:
Dhankuta: 
&#x2022;	1,400 HHs are expected to benefit in Dhankuta municipality
&#x2022;	Waste segregation plant platform is initiated
&#x2022;	School level and community level orientation is completed
&#x2022;	Waste bins procurement is initiated
&#x2022;	Exposure visit is taken a place to Guwahati, Asam, India for the municipal authorities for the best practices in municipal waste management.
Ghorahi Sub-metropolitan City:
&#x2022;	LOA is made with the municipality
&#x2022;	As private sector is already building a huge waste management plant, UNDP support is expected to benefit for 1,550 HHs for household biogas facility 
&#x2022;	Need assessment of 8 hospitals carried out with the close consultation with Department of Health Services (DoHS)/Ministry of Health and Population, further collaboration is being done with selected 4 hospitals for the medical waste management is being taken a place
&#x2022;	Partnership agreement is established with 2 local governments (Karjanha Municipality and Lumbini Buddhist university/Devdaha Municipality)
&#x2022;	Agroforest and multilayer plantation in 70 Hectare (60 hectare in Karjanha and 10 hectares in Devdaha/LBU) of degraded and fallow land
&#x2022;	Selection of 343 beneficiary HHs, (of which 60% women 44% beneficiaries are from Dalit community and is provisioned)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
